### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### api-keys.http — Inbound API Key (Personal Access Token) Contract
### Validates create / list / authenticate-with / revoke for user-owned API keys.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Authenticate (session token — the bearer the BFF forwards)
# @name login
POST {{$dotenv ROUTER_URL}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{$dotenv ADMIN_EMAIL}}",
  "password": "{{$dotenv ADMIN_PASSWORD}}"
}

?? status == 200

###

### REST — Create an API key (plaintext secret returned exactly once)
# @name createKey
POST {{$dotenv ROUTER_URL}}/api/v1/api-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{login.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "e2e-contract-key"
}

?? status == 201

###

### REST — List API keys (metadata only, never the secret)
# @name listKeys
GET {{$dotenv ROUTER_URL}}/api/v1/api-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{login.token}}

?? status == 200

###

### REST — Authenticate a protected endpoint with the API key itself
# @name callWithKey
GET {{$dotenv ROUTER_URL}}/api/v1/features
Authorization: Bearer {{createKey.key}}

?? status == 200

###

### REST — Revoke the API key
# @name revokeKey
DELETE {{$dotenv ROUTER_URL}}/api/v1/api-keys/{{createKey.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.token}}

?? status == 204

###

### REST — The revoked key is now rejected
# @name callAfterRevoke
GET {{$dotenv ROUTER_URL}}/api/v1/features
Authorization: Bearer {{createKey.key}}

?? status == 401
